{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"23f77cf2360a40888ebb9b4712c89661c8cc7049a6ffbde0cc0095c083b3b92a","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_22c7f228a2134ebd066d61f25873bfcddee8a47a01a356b36c5132579856aea7","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical application of GANs to steganography. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine compliance with specific venue anonymity policies, plagiarism status, or broader impact policy requirements. Visible ethical considerations are limited to the dual-use nature of the technology, while data usage involves a public dataset and copyrighted text excerpts without explicit licensing details.","paper_id":"H1hoFU9xe","paper_identity_sha256":"72c2985da7230e235a6dcfd15eb15d845e00fd5cbe3e49a02a60464a7bec357e","prompt_identity_sha256":"eb93c9b27977e83fae6837abd1312c09b80ee6bd3ba73d3c84610a25c697eea3","raw_response_sha256":"314f8583258352c9b475a757ad08b32b006aef7a25028629925ec57bc4db15f1","request_identity_sha256":"de60ac87c53dc4dafeb895475b8c7c67de29818289f3430e57585ba1bd92e790","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"d76b6556207550a22d2454c795ae1048b8c67bdba4b9f2c4eac07355ee06eda5","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-018"],"review_text":"The paper proposes a method to generate images that evade steganalysis, which is a dual-use technology capable of facilitating the concealment of illicit information. The authors acknowledge the potential for misuse by stating the model 'can be used in steganographic applications' and demonstrating its ability to 'deceive the steganography analyzer.' However, the paper does not include a dedicated discussion on ethical risks, potential harms to society, or mitigation strategies for malicious use. The focus remains strictly on the technical efficacy of deceiving classifiers, without addressing the broader ethical implications of reducing the detectability of hidden messages.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-013","SRC-014"],"review_text":"The experiments utilize the Celebrities dataset, which contains images of public figures, and excerpts from The New York Times for embedding. The paper does not provide details regarding the licensing terms of the Celebrities dataset or whether the use of The New York Times text complies with copyright or fair use policies. There is no mention of consent from the individuals depicted in the images or specific privacy compliance measures beyond the standard use of a public academic dataset. The evidence is insufficient to confirm adherence to specific data privacy regulations or licensing agreements for the text and image sources.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors' names (Denis Volkhonskiy, Boris Borisenko, Evgeny Burnaev), their institutional affiliations (Skolkovo Institute of Science and Technology, Kharkevich Institute, HSE), and their email addresses. While this is standard for published versions, the supplied evidence does not include a frozen venue anonymity policy for the specific submission context to determine if this constitutes a double-blind violation. Therefore, no policy violation or clearance can be declared based solely on the visible text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied paper text does not contain explicit disclosures of plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. There is no auditable evidence of textual or figure overlap with other works, nor any statement indicating simultaneous submission to other venues. As the corpus build lacks frozen plagiarism-overlap evidence, the absence of such disclosures in the text is insufficient to prove originality or the absence of dual submission.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-022"],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit documentation of IRB/ethics approvals. The conclusion section focuses on technical contributions and future work, without addressing the societal implications of the technology. Without a frozen policy obligation requiring these specific documents for this venue and year, the absence of such statements cannot be declared a compliance failure, but the paper does not provide evidence of having completed any required impact assessments.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"61750717b34c08fcb9dd5a454bbb62d67b084257fa23ae7826679fd68cd9a2cb","paper_id":"H1hoFU9xe","paper_ordinal":92,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"314f8583258352c9b475a757ad08b32b006aef7a25028629925ec57bc4db15f1","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"H1hoFU9xe","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"40f7833cdfb6befe9a6b3ed1947f927ee98d997d9e0d244eec55591ff74a1321","request_identity_sha256":"de60ac87c53dc4dafeb895475b8c7c67de29818289f3430e57585ba1bd92e790","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":847,"prompt_tokens":12968,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":13815},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"de60ac87c53dc4dafeb895475b8c7c67de29818289f3430e57585ba1bd92e790","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}